        "source_type": "text",
        "source_sentence": "The glass transition temperature $( T _ { \\mathrm { g } } )$of the pure polymer was measured with a Mettler 821 calorimetric system. Polymer sample was dried under reduced pressure in a vacuum oven prior to measurement. Dry nitrogen was used as purge gas and thermogram was measured in the range 308– 523 K at a scan rate of 20 $\\mathrm { K } \\mathrm { m i n } ^ { - 1 }$."
      },
      "confidence": {
        "score": 0.9
      }
    },
    {
      "condition_id": "mc002",
      "other_conditions": {
        "frequency_range": "10⁻¹ to 10⁸ Hz",
        "temperature_step": "5 K",
        "sample_shape": "disc-shaped, diameter 20 and 10 mm"
      },
      "other_condition_evidence": {},
      "condition_status": "reported",
      "evidence": {
        "block_id": "P_1_25",
        "page": 1,
        "bbox": [
          526.0,
          619.0,
          922.0,
          773.0
        ],
        "source_type": "text",
        "source_sentence": "Dielectric measurements were carried out by means of a Novocontrol Broad Band Dielectric Spectrometer made up of an Alpha analyzer to carry out measurement from $1 0 ^ { - 1 } ~ \\mathrm { t o } ~ 1 0 ^ { 6 }$Hz and an Agilent 4991A RF analyzer to perform measurements from ${ 1 0 } ^ { 6 }$to ${ 1 0 } ^ { 8 }$Hz, both devices being coupled with a Quatro temperature controller. Isothermal measurements were carried out from 148 to 423 K in 5-K steps on a molded, disc-shaped (diameter of 20 and 10 mm, respectively) sample."
      },
      "confidence": {
        "score": 0.9
      }
    }
  ],
